# Menus, roles & permissions

All future admin features MUST use the existing menu + permission system. Do not build parallel RBAC.

## When adding a new admin page or feature

1. Add row to `platform_menus` (migration) with `permission` (e.g. `patients:read`)
2. Grant via role/user menu editors with `allowed_actions[]`
3. Page: `requirePermission(supabase, 'resource:read')` — redirect `/admin?error=no_permission` on deny
4. Server actions: `requirePermission` for create/update/delete/approve
5. UI: `useAdminWorkspace().can('resource:action')` to hide/disable buttons
6. Menu appears in sidebar only if assigned to user/role

## Permission resolution

- `resolveUserPermissions()` / `buildEffectivePermissionSet()` in `src/lib/menus/permissions.ts`
- Admin role = full access
- Others = union of grants from `role_menu_grants` or `user_menu_grants` (custom mode)

## Denied message

Use `PERMISSION_DENIED_MESSAGE` from `src/lib/auth/errors.ts` — never invent new copy.

